.TH "COMPLYCTL" "1" "August 2026" "Complyctl Manual"
.SH NAME
complyctl \- compliance assessment CLI using provider\-based scanning
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]complyctl\f[R] [command] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Complyctl is a lightweight compliance runtime that pulls Gemara policies
from an OCI registry and executes scans via providers, producing
compliance reports in multiple formats (EvaluationLog, OSCAL, SARIF,
Markdown).
.SS Providers
Providers are standalone executables that integrate complyctl with
policy engines such as OpenSCAP, Ampel, and OPA.
Each provider converts policy content into the engine\(cqs native input
format and translates the raw results back into the schema used by
complyctl for report generation.
.PP
Providers communicate with complyctl via gRPC and can be authored in any
language.
They are distributed separately (e.g., via the
\f[B]complytime\-providers\f[R] package) and discovered automatically by
naming convention (\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-*\f[R]) from the following
directories:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]\(ti/.local/share/complytime/providers/\f[R] (user directory, takes
precedence)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]/usr/libexec/complytime/providers/\f[R] (system directory)
.PP
Run \f[B]complyctl providers\f[R] to list discovered providers on your
system and \f[B]complyctl doctor\f[R] to validate the full stack
including provider health and variable requirements.
.PP
See the complytime\-providers repository at \c
.UR https://github.com/complytime/complytime-providers
.UE \c
\ for available providers and their documentation.
See the provider authoring guide at \c
.UR https://github.com/complytime/complytime-providers/blob/main/docs/provider-guide.md
.UE \c
\ for writing custom providers.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
Create a workspace configuration file
(\f[B].complytime/complytime.yaml\f[R]).
Interactively prompts for policies and targets.
Errors if the configuration file already exists.
.IP
.EX
complyctl init
.EE
.SS get
Fetch policies and complypacks from OCI registries into the local cache.
Performs incremental sync \(em only downloads new or modified content.
Uses Docker credential helpers for authentication.
.IP
.EX
complyctl get
complyctl get \-\-skip\-verify
.EE
.TP
\f[B]\-t\f[R], \f[B]\(entimeout\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Maximum time for the get operation (default: \f[B]5m\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-verify\f[R]
Skip signature verification for fetched artifacts.
.SS list
List cached Gemara policies with their evaluator, control count, digest,
and verification status.
.IP
.EX
complyctl list
complyctl list \-\-policy\-id nist\-800\-53\-r5
.EE
.TP
\f[B]\(enpolicy\-id\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
Filter output to a single policy.
.SS generate
Resolve the policy dependency graph from cache, extract assessment
configurations, apply parameter overrides from
\f[B]complytime.yaml\f[R], and dispatch to the matching provider via the
Generate RPC.
.IP
.EX
complyctl generate \-\-policy\-id nist\-800\-53\-r5
.EE
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R], \f[B]\(enpolicy\-id\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
Policy ID to generate (\f[B]required\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\-t\f[R], \f[B]\(entimeout\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Maximum time for the generate operation (default: \f[B]5m\f[R]).
.SS scan
Scan targets and produce compliance reports.
When a target is specified and references exactly one policy,
\f[B]\(enpolicy\-id\f[R] is inferred.
At least one of \f[I][target]\f[R] or \f[B]\(enpolicy\-id\f[R] is
required.
.PP
Output is written to \f[B].complytime/scan/\f[R].
.IP
.EX
complyctl scan \-\-policy\-id my\-policy
complyctl scan my\-target
complyctl scan my\-target \-\-policy\-id my\-policy \-\-format pretty
complyctl scan \-\-policy\-id my\-policy \-\-log\-format json
.EE
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R], \f[B]\(enpolicy\-id\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
Policy ID to scan.
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\(enformat\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
Additional output format: \f[B]oscal\f[R], \f[B]pretty\f[R] (Markdown),
\f[B]sarif\f[R].
The default EvaluationLog is always produced regardless of this flag.
.TP
\f[B]\-t\f[R], \f[B]\(entimeout\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Maximum time for the scan operation (default: \f[B]5m\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\(enshow\-passing\f[R]
Include passing controls in the terminal scan summary table (default:
\f[B]true\f[R]).
Can also be set via \f[B]COMPLYTIME_SHOW_PASSING\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\(enlog\-format\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
EvaluationLog serialization format: \f[B]yaml\f[R], \f[B]json\f[R]
(default: \f[B]yaml\f[R]).
Can also be set via \f[B]COMPLYTIME_LOG_FORMAT\f[R].
.SS doctor
Run pre\-flight diagnostics on the workspace.
Checks provider discovery, policy cache integrity, configuration
validation, complypack availability, and cache health (disk usage,
orphaned versions).
.IP
.EX
complyctl doctor
complyctl doctor \-\-verbose
complyctl doctor \-\-format text
complyctl doctor \-\-format json
.EE
.TP
\f[B]\(enverbose\f[R]
Expand per\-provider variable detail.
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\(enformat\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
Output format: \f[B]human\f[R] (emoji, default), \f[B]text\f[R]
(grep\-friendly plain labels: [PASS]/[FAIL]/[WARN]), \f[B]json\f[R]
(structured machine output).
When \f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R] is set, \f[B]text\f[R] is selected
automatically.
.SS providers
List discovered scanning providers with their evaluator ID, path, health
status, version, and cached complypack versions.
.IP
.EX
complyctl providers
.EE
.SS version
Print the version.
.IP
.EX
complyctl version
.EE
.SS completion
Generate shell completion scripts for Bash, Zsh, Fish, or PowerShell.
.IP
.EX
complyctl completion bash
complyctl completion zsh
complyctl completion fish
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
These options apply to all commands.
.TP
\f[B]\-d\f[R], \f[B]\(endebug\f[R]
Output debug logs to stderr and the workspace log file.
.TP
\f[B]\-w\f[R], \f[B]\(enworkspace\f[R] \f[I]directory\f[R]
Workspace directory.
Defaults to the current directory.
Can also be set via \f[B]COMPLYTIME_WORKSPACE\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\(enhelp\f[R]
Show help for complyctl or any subcommand.
.PP
Run \f[B]complyctl [command] \(enhelp\f[R] for more information about a
specific command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]COMPLYTIME_WORKSPACE\f[R]
Override the workspace directory used by complyctl.
When set, complyctl resolves configuration and output paths relative to
this directory.
The \f[B]\(enworkspace\f[R] flag takes precedence.
.TP
\f[B]COMPLYTIME_SHOW_PASSING\f[R]
When set to \f[B]false\f[R], exclude passing controls from the terminal
scan summary table.
Default: \f[B]true\f[R] (show all controls).
The \f[B]\(enshow\-passing\f[R] flag takes precedence.
.TP
\f[B]COMPLYTIME_LOG_FORMAT\f[R]
EvaluationLog serialization format: \f[B]yaml\f[R] or \f[B]json\f[R].
Default: \f[B]yaml\f[R].
The \f[B]\(enlog\-format\f[R] flag takes precedence.
.TP
\f[B]COMPLYTIME_CACHE_VERSIONS\f[R]
Number of complypack versions to retain per evaluator\-id in the local
cache (\(ti/.cache/complytime/complypacks/).
Default: \f[B]1\f[R].
Values less than 1 are clamped to 1.
.TP
\f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R]
When set (any non\-empty value), \f[B]complyctl doctor\f[R]
automatically selects \f[B]text\f[R] format instead of the default
human\-readable emoji output.
Follows the NO_COLOR convention at https://no\-color.org.
Has no effect when \f[B]\(enformat\f[R] is specified explicitly.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Command completed successfully.
Scan findings (passed, failed, not applicable) are reported in the
output but do not affect the exit code.
Policy findings are data, not errors.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
An operational error occurred.
This includes provider failures, invalid configuration, or zero
requirements assessed.
Reports and summaries are written before the non\-zero exit so partial
results remain available.
.PP
To gate a pipeline on compliance results, parse the scan output (SARIF,
OSCAL) with your policy engine rather than relying on the exit code.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.cache/complytime/policies/\f[R]
OCI Layout cache for fetched policies (one store per policy ID).
Follows the XDG Base Directory Specification
(\f[B]$XDG_CACHE_HOME\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.cache/complytime/complypacks/\f[R]
Complypack cache with version retention per evaluator\-id.
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.local/share/complytime/state.json\f[R]
Digest tracking for incremental policy sync.
Follows the XDG Base Directory Specification (\f[B]$XDG_DATA_HOME\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.local/share/complytime/providers/\f[R]
User\-installed provider executables (takes precedence over system
directory).
.TP
\f[B]/usr/libexec/complytime/providers/\f[R]
System\-installed provider executables.
.TP
\f[B].complytime/complytime.yaml\f[R]
Workspace configuration file (policies, targets, variables).
.TP
\f[B].complytime/scan/\f[R]
Scan output reports (EvaluationLog, OSCAL, SARIF, Markdown).
.TP
\f[B].complytime/complyctl.log\f[R]
Debug log file (created when \f[B]\(endebug\f[R] is used).
